    "body": "## What happens?\n\n`INSERT OR REPLACE` silently fails to update existing rows on certain database files. The statement executes without error, but the data is not modified. The same operation works correctly with `INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE SET`.\n\n## To Reproduce\n\nThe bug appears to be specific to certain database files and I haven't been able to reproduce it with a fresh database. However, here's what I observe:\n\n```python\nimport duckdb\n\n# On the affected database file:\nconn = duckdb.connect('affected_database.duckdb')\n\n# This fails silently - data is NOT updated\nconn.execute('''\n    INSERT OR REPLACE INTO my_table (id, col1, col2, col3)\n    VALUES ('existing_id', 'new_val1', 'new_val2', 'new_val3')\n''')\n\n# Verify: values are UNCHANGED (bug!)\nresult = conn.execute(\"SELECT * FROM my_table WHERE id = 'existing_id'\").fetchone()\n# Returns OLD values, not new ones\n\n# Workaround that DOES work:\nconn.execute('''\n    INSERT INTO my_table (id, col1, col2, col3)\n    VALUES ('existing_id', 'new_val1', 'new_val2', 'new_val3')\n    ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET \n        col1 = excluded.col1,\n        col2 = excluded.col2,\n        col3 = excluded.col3\n''')\n# This correctly updates the row\n```\n\n## Schema of affected table\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE aggregation_documents (\n    document_id VARCHAR NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,\n    url VARCHAR NOT NULL,\n    timestamp VARCHAR NOT NULL,\n    ner_entity_count BIGINT,\n    coreference_mentions_added BIGINT,\n    total_mentions BIGINT,\n    primary_entity VARCHAR,\n    primary_entity_count BIGINT,\n    primary_changed BIGINT DEFAULT 0,\n    previous_primary VARCHAR,\n    batch_id VARCHAR,\n    consolidated_counts JSON NOT NULL,\n    pipeline_name VARCHAR NOT NULL DEFAULT 'default'\n);\nCREATE INDEX idx_agg_url ON aggregation_documents(url);\nCREATE INDEX idx_agg_pipeline ON aggregation_documents(pipeline_name);\n```\n\n## Observations\n\n1. The bug is **silent** - no error is raised, the execute() call succeeds\n2. The bug is **consistent** - `INSERT OR REPLACE` never works on the affected database\n3. `CHECKPOINT` and `VACUUM` do not fix the issue\n4. `INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE SET` works correctly as a workaround\n5. Fresh databases with identical schema work correctly with `INSERT OR REPLACE`\n6. The affected database was created over multiple sessions with inserts, updates, and deletes\n\n## OS\n\nLinux 6.17.0-8-generic (Ubuntu)\n\n## DuckDB Version\n\n1.4.2\n\n## DuckDB Client\n\nPython 3.13.9\n\n## Hardware\n\nx86_64\n\n## Full Name\n\nAndrea Moro\n\n## Affiliation\n\nPersonal project\n\n## Have you tried this on the latest `main` branch?\n\n- [ ] I have tested with a `main` build\n\n## Have you tried the steps to reproduce? Do they include all relevant data and configuration?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have",
